# transpose.keys -- exercises step 5 of build/plans/isocline.rst:
# ic_enable_transpose_gosling(), enabled unconditionally in jig.c's
# run_child_readline_loop() (no existing test used ctrl-T before this,
# so this is safe to turn on for every ".keys" test).
#
# "ab", ctrl-T at end of line: with the Gosling behavior enabled this
# swaps the last two characters ("ab" -> "ba") instead of doing
# nothing (the plain sbuf_swap_char() end-of-line guard).  Typing "c"
# then gives "bac".
i 2
+ ab
k C-T
+ c
#
# One LEFT puts the cursor between 'a' and 'c' (not at the end), so
# the next ctrl-T takes the ordinary (non-Gosling) path: it swaps the
# characters immediately before and after the cursor, "bac" -> "bca",
# leaving the cursor between 'c' and 'a'.
k LEFT
k C-T
k ENTER
w 20
#
# Confirm what was actually committed by dumping the history (see
# keybind.keys for the ctrl-X binding and the blank-placeholder-at-
# index-0 caveat): index 1 should read "bca".
k C-X
w 20
q
